  ('2bfeb49e-90d9-5537-aed9-66bbccff09b2', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'combinatorics-probability'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Five people, including Kai and Lee, sit in a row of $5$ chairs in a random order. What is the probability that Kai and Lee do NOT sit next to each other?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{3}{5}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{1}{2}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-two-equally-likely-outcomes"},{"text":"$\\frac{2}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-probability-of-sitting-together"},{"text":"$\\frac{4}{5}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-the-pair-can-swap"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{3}{5}$$q$, $q$Treat Kai and Lee as one block: $4!$ arrangements of the block and the other $3$ people, times $2$ orders inside the block, gives $48$ seating orders with them together. Out of $5! = 120$ orders, the probability they sit together is $\frac{48}{120} = \frac{2}{5}$, so the probability they do not is $1 - \frac{2}{5} = \frac{3}{5}$. The value $\frac{4}{5}$ counts only $24$ together orders, forgetting that Kai and Lee can switch seats.$q$, 'draft', null)
