  ('b8d679bd-17c2-573d-a3cf-3023146cbe87', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'combinatorics-probability'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A committee of $3$ is chosen at random from $8$ students, including Mia and Noor. What is the probability that both Mia and Noor are on the committee?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$\\frac{1}{56}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"treated-favorable-as-one-committee"},{"text":"$\\frac{5}{14}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"found-probability-of-neither"},{"text":"$\\frac{3}{28}$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$\\frac{9}{64}$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"assumed-independent-selections"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$\frac{3}{28}$$q$, $q$There are $_8C_3 = 56$ committees. If Mia and Noor are both on it, the third seat goes to one of the other $6$ students, so there are $6$ favorable committees and the probability is $\frac{6}{56} = \frac{3}{28}$. The value $\frac{1}{56}$ forgets that the third member can be any of $6$ students.$q$, 'draft', null)
